{
  "$comment": "The naming contract, as cases. Hand-authored and committed, NOT generated. Two implementations of the same rules — alkera_core.files.names (the server, and the authority) and @alkera/chat-model's names.ts (the field) — are each driven through every case by their own suite, so a field that refuses locally and a server that refuses on the wire cannot disagree about which rule was broken. A rule change edits this file and both implementations in the same commit; nothing regenerates it. Names are text here, so only cases expressible as valid UTF-8 live in it; the server's byte-level corpus stays in packages/api-core/tests/fixtures/files/.",
